{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02JT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-dimension-function}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6223d313a52fde6daa657604175c4733b1b0b8dd67889657e02b18de2cace673", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn application is the construction of a dimension function\non any scheme of finite type over a universally catenary\nscheme endowed with a dimension function. For the definition\nof dimension functions, see\nTopology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:384a06bb9f6d66841141d045ac9eaf1bfc37eea85b12443c9ad4bed55a2562c2", "unit_id": "tag:02JT:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02JT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\delta : S \\to \\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "\\begin{align*}\n\\delta = \\delta_{X/S} : X & \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{Z} \\\\\nx & \\longmapsto \\delta(f(x)) + \\text{trdeg}_{\\kappa(f(x))} \\kappa(x)\n\\end{align*}", "MATH_0006": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-dimension-function-propagates}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:49ffc547150a7ff955e75d66047ecdcbdda8f782638d68372bac6ed04b554b18", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:38b26c292318f3f6d5df226736b0e607e9e66760e1ca5d7a94888850dd9314b8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian and universally catenary scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a dimension function.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of schemes.\nAssume <MATH_0004> locally of finite type.\nThen the map\n<MATH_0005>\nis a dimension function on <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:56e14f6d06225368f73eb90a91c4bac616a7828a165b10c00d3adfad8d41a419", "unit_id": "tag:02JW:statement"}
